('05b46003-d3a7-57b2-81a7-47c52fc55c52'::uuid,'est2','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'easy','mcq','"The function below can be used to model the area of a rectangle in square inches, A, if the rectangle has a perimeter of 72 inches and a width of w inches.\nA = 36w − w²\nIn this situation, which of the following best describes the domain of the function?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"0 < w < 6"},{"key":"G","text":"0 < w < 72"},{"key":"H","text":"0 < w < 18"},{"key":"J","text":"0 < w < 36"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-20","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"J"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-20)."'::jsonb),
('b98f8bc6-72a7-52f0-9fbd-c021e38977b6'::uuid,'est2','"Rational, Radical, Exponential & Logarithmic Functions"'::jsonb,'hard','mcq','"What is the inverse of h(x) = (1/2)log₃(x) ?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"h⁻¹(x) = 3^(2x)"},{"key":"B","text":"h⁻¹(x) = 2(3)^x"},{"key":"C","text":"h⁻¹(x) = 2(log_x 3)"},{"key":"D","text":"h⁻¹(x) = log₃(2x)"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-21","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Rational, Radical, Exponential & Logarithmic Functions"}'::jsonb,'"A"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-21)."'::jsonb),
('8762d49a-aef5-58e9-b624-f02b6cb1d7f6'::uuid,'est2','"Polynomials & Quadratic Functions"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"A table of values for the quadratic function g is shown below.\n[Table — x | g(x): −1|−55, 2|−16, 5|5, 6|8, 9|5, 10|0, 12|−16, 14|−40]\nWhich of the following statements about the graph of g are true?\nI. The graph has a line of symmetry at x = 7.\nII. The graph has a y-intercept at (0, −40).\nIII. The graph has an x-intercept at (4, 0).\nIV. The graph has a vertex at (6, 8)."'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"I and II only"},{"key":"G","text":"III and IV only"},{"key":"H","text":"I, II, and III only"},{"key":"J","text":"I, II, III, and IV"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-22","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Polynomials & Quadratic Functions"}'::jsonb,'"H"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-22)."'::jsonb),
('0a0c5f96-98da-59bb-be47-17a32af0555b'::uuid,'est2','"Algebra Foundations, Equations & Inequalities"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The product of 2 consecutive odd integers is 483. If x represents the smaller integer, which equation can be used to find both integers?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"x(x + 2) = 483"},{"key":"B","text":"x(x + 1) = 483"},{"key":"C","text":"x(x + 3) = 483"},{"key":"D","text":"(x + 1)(x + 2) = 483"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-23","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Algebra Foundations, Equations & Inequalities"}'::jsonb,'"A"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-23)."'::jsonb),
('61deb22b-a7ff-5d3b-a85c-c37a7def7abf'::uuid,'est2','"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"'::jsonb,'medium','numeric','"If 5 is an element in the domain of f(x) = (7x − 22)/4, what is the corresponding element in the range?\nRecord your answer and fill in the bubbles on your answer document. [Griddable — answer: 3.25]"'::jsonb,'[]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-24","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"}'::jsonb,'"3.25"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-24)."'::jsonb),
('a96fed27-40be-507c-905d-6dd1189de759'::uuid,'est2','"Sequences, Complex Numbers & Advanced Algebra"'::jsonb,'hard','mcq','"The roots of a quadratic equation are given by the expression below.\n(−25 ± √(−100))/25\nWhich of the following is an equivalent expression?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"−1 ± (2i)/5"},{"key":"B","text":"−1 ± 2i"},{"key":"C","text":"−25 ± (2i)/5"},{"key":"D","text":"−25 ± 2i"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-25","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Sequences, Complex Numbers & Advanced Algebra"}'::jsonb,'"A"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-25)."'::jsonb),
('d15bc454-978f-524f-9083-da89e564095b'::uuid,'est2','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'easy','mcq','"An antibiotic is introduced into a colony of 12,000 bacteria during a laboratory experiment. The function below can be used to model the number of bacteria in the colony after m minutes.\nn(m) = 12,000(0.851)^(m/10)\nWhich value is closest to the amount of time needed for the population of the colony to drop to 8,000 bacteria?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"11 min"},{"key":"G","text":"25 min"},{"key":"H","text":"8 min"},{"key":"J","text":"42 min"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-26","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"G"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-26)."'::jsonb),
('91b40ebb-946a-509e-9e22-cd8ea57d7272'::uuid,'est2','"Polynomials & Quadratic Functions"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The table below shows values of a quadratic function g.\n[Table — x | g(x): −5|−11, −4|8, −3|21, −2|28, −1|29, 0|24, 1|13, 2|−4, 3|−27]\nBased on the table, in which interval can a solution to g(x) = 0 be found?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"−5 < x < −4"},{"key":"B","text":"−2 < x < −1"},{"key":"C","text":"−1 < x < 1"},{"key":"D","text":"2 < x < 3"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-27","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Polynomials & Quadratic Functions"}'::jsonb,'"A"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-27)."'::jsonb),
('7a42059f-3156-54ab-b7fe-cbafc43c256a'::uuid,'est2','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'easy','mcq','"The given function models the equivalent resistance in ohms, R, when a fixed 9-ohm resistor is connected in parallel with a variable resistor of x ohms.\nR = 9x/(9 + x)\nWhich value of x is closest to the number of ohms needed in the variable resistor for there to be an equivalent resistance, R, of 6.4 ohms?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"15.4"},{"key":"G","text":"57.6"},{"key":"H","text":"3.7"},{"key":"J","text":"22.2"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-28","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"J"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-28)."'::jsonb),
('d066a625-8ab5-520e-b408-9500344c3141'::uuid,'est2','"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"For the functions h and g, which statement is true if h(x) = g(x + 14) − 12 ?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"The graph of h is the result of the graph of g being translated right 14 units and down 12 units."},{"key":"B","text":"The graph of h is the result of the graph of g being translated left 14 units and down 12 units."},{"key":"C","text":"The graph of h is the result of the graph of g being translated right 14 units and up 12 units."},{"key":"D","text":"The graph of h is the result of the graph of g being translated left 14 units and up 12 units."}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-29","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-29)."'::jsonb),
('f3c606d2-2273-58b1-97db-44fd0e92b79b'::uuid,'est2','"Rational, Radical, Exponential & Logarithmic Functions"'::jsonb,'hard','mcq','"The graph of the exponential function f is shown on the grid below.\n[Figure: Increasing exponential passing through (−2, 16) and (0, 32), asymptote y = 0 on the left.]\nFor what values of x is f(x) > 16 ?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"x > −2"},{"key":"G","text":"x > 0"},{"key":"H","text":"−2 < x < 2"},{"key":"J","text":"∞ < x < −2"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-30","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Rational, Radical, Exponential & Logarithmic Functions","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/MA-30.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for MA-30","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"F"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-30)."'::jsonb),
('fbf7c3b2-6297-5c45-86f7-02def9dc0044'::uuid,'est2','"Rational, Radical, Exponential & Logarithmic Functions"'::jsonb,'medium','numeric','"What value of n makes √(10 − 3n) = 7 true?\nRecord your answer and fill in the bubbles on your answer document. [Griddable — answer: −13]"'::jsonb,'[]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-31","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Rational, Radical, Exponential & Logarithmic Functions"}'::jsonb,'"−13"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-31)."'::jsonb),
('b4e5ce8d-f15e-510b-ad83-cc6af287f0df'::uuid,'est2','"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which equation has the same graph as 2x² − 4x − y + 11 = 0 ?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"y = (2x − 1)² + 9"},{"key":"G","text":"y = (2x − 1)² + 13"},{"key":"H","text":"y = 2(x − 1)² + 9"},{"key":"J","text":"y = 2(x − 1)² + 13"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-32","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"}'::jsonb,'"H"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-32)."'::jsonb),
('72df728c-ffd5-502b-80ec-c9ee8bb5148f'::uuid,'est2','"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"A sector of a circle is shown below.\n[Figure: Quarter-circle sector with both radii labeled r and a right angle at the center.]\nThe area, A, of the sector is π/4 times the square of the radius, r. Which graph represents this relationship?\n[Figure: Four graphs of Area vs Radius. A: decreasing curve. B: increasing curve bending upward from the origin. C: decreasing curve leveling off. D: increasing curve leveling off.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"Graph A"},{"key":"B","text":"Graph B"},{"key":"C","text":"Graph C"},{"key":"D","text":"Graph D"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-33","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/MA-33.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for MA-33","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-33)."'::jsonb),
('74d3632e-c237-598f-9070-117b6cfb5be4'::uuid,'est2','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The hypotenuse of a right triangle is 17 inches long. A leg of this triangle, y, is 1 inch less than twice the length of the other leg, x. Which system of equations can be used to determine the lengths of the 2 legs of this right triangle in inches?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"x² + y² = 289 ; y = 2x − 1"},{"key":"G","text":"x² + y² = 289 ; 2x + y = 1"},{"key":"H","text":"x + y = 17 ; y = 2x − 1"},{"key":"J","text":"x + y = 17 ; 2x + y = 1"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-34","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"}'::jsonb,'"F"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-34)."'::jsonb),
('c6c9fda8-815d-5a8d-9643-c26b58b79078'::uuid,'est2','"Sequences, Complex Numbers & Advanced Algebra"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"What is the solution set for x² + 4 = 6x ?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"{−3 ± i√14}"},{"key":"B","text":"{−3 ± √5}"},{"key":"C","text":"{3 ± i√14}"},{"key":"D","text":"{3 ± √5}"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-35","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Sequences, Complex Numbers & Advanced Algebra"}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-35)."'::jsonb),
('1ff74972-0a58-5b33-bfe3-899f8becb55b'::uuid,'est2','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'hard','mcq','"A plane intersects a double cone as shown below.\n[Figure: A vertical plane slicing through both nappes of a double cone.]\nWhat conic section is created by this intersection?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"Circle"},{"key":"G","text":"Ellipse"},{"key":"H","text":"Hyperbola"},{"key":"J","text":"Parabola"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh.md","source_sha256":"f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20","source_question_id":"MA-36","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/MA-36.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for MA-36","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"H"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh.md (MA-36)."'::jsonb),
