('648b977a-3108-53b4-bc7d-52cfb915e0f7'::uuid,'est2','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which expression can be used to find the length of QR in centimeters?\n[Figure: Right triangle QRS with right angle at R, RS = 19 cm, angle S = 20°.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"19(cos 20°)"},{"key":"B","text":"19(tan 20°)"},{"key":"C","text":"19(sin 70°)"},{"key":"D","text":"19(tan 70°)"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh_geo.md","source_sha256":"fd550cf9acb0c34c08b3bebd88f0b67714179fd7b1d4644f694d4388df535983","source_question_id":"MG-23","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/MG-23.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for MG-23","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh_geo.md (MG-23)."'::jsonb),
('a5d554f4-9162-53e1-ba6b-73b0726b9a65'::uuid,'est2','"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"In circle E below, ∠AEB ≅ ∠CED.\n[Figure: Circle with center E; A at top, D at bottom (AD a diameter-like vertical chord through E), B and C on the right side; radii EB and EC drawn.]\nBased on this information, which statement must be true?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"AB ≅ CD"},{"key":"G","text":"EB ⊥ EC"},{"key":"H","text":"m∠AED = 4(m∠DEC)"},{"key":"J","text":"m∠AEB + m∠DEC = m∠BEC"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh_geo.md","source_sha256":"fd550cf9acb0c34c08b3bebd88f0b67714179fd7b1d4644f694d4388df535983","source_question_id":"MG-24","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/MG-24.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for MG-24","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"F"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh_geo.md (MG-24)."'::jsonb),
('81994396-4945-566c-8baf-8516a90d18a7'::uuid,'est2','"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The graph of line g is shown below.\n[Figure: Line g passing through (−4, 6) and (4, 2).]\nWhich equation describes a line parallel to line g that has a y-intercept at (0, −1)?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"y = 2x − 1"},{"key":"B","text":"y = (1/2)x − 1"},{"key":"C","text":"y = −(1/2)x − 1"},{"key":"D","text":"y = −2x − 1"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh_geo.md","source_sha256":"fd550cf9acb0c34c08b3bebd88f0b67714179fd7b1d4644f694d4388df535983","source_question_id":"MG-25","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/MG-25.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for MG-25","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh_geo.md (MG-25)."'::jsonb),
('2d5cd099-29e5-5b4c-80f6-62821c77b365'::uuid,'est2','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'medium','numeric','"Three gears in a machine are positioned relative to each other to form an isosceles right triangle, as shown below.\n[Figure: Three gears with centers A, B, C forming an isosceles right triangle with the right angle at B; AC = 9.1√2 cm.]\nWhat is the distance in centimeters between the centers of the gears located at B and C?\nRecord your answer and fill in the bubbles on your answer document. [Griddable — answer: 9.1]"'::jsonb,'[]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh_geo.md","source_sha256":"fd550cf9acb0c34c08b3bebd88f0b67714179fd7b1d4644f694d4388df535983","source_question_id":"MG-26","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/MG-26.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for MG-26","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"9.1"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh_geo.md (MG-26)."'::jsonb),
('2830cdda-eb5d-5205-849b-f45b71e0884d'::uuid,'est2','"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The following conditional statement is true.\n\"If a quadrilateral is a square, then it has four congruent sides.\"\nWhich statement must also be true?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"If a quadrilateral has four congruent sides, then it is a square."},{"key":"B","text":"If a quadrilateral does not have four congruent sides, then it is not a square."},{"key":"C","text":"If a quadrilateral is not a square, then it does not have four congruent sides."},{"key":"D","text":"If a quadrilateral does not have four congruent sides, then it is a square."}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"moh_geo.md","source_sha256":"fd550cf9acb0c34c08b3bebd88f0b67714179fd7b1d4644f694d4388df535983","source_question_id":"MG-27","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from moh_geo.md (MG-27)."'::jsonb),
